## Investigation Summary: TinyMCE Component Picker Architecture

### (1) **Controlling Files & Symbols**

| File | Purpose | Key Symbols |
|------|---------|------------|
| [renderers/tinymce/src/plugins/components.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/plugins/components.ts) | Plugin factory & picker logic | `createComponentsPlugin()`, `buildComponentList()`, `ComponentsPickerOptions` |
| [renderers/tinymce/src/cssdoc/model.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/cssdoc/model.ts) | Merged cssdoc model | `MERGED_MODEL`, `listComponents()`, `findEntry()`, `CssDocEntry` |
| [renderers/tinymce/src/plugins/pantoken.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/plugins/pantoken.ts) | Meta-plugin composing all pickers | `createPantokenPlugin()`, `PantokenPluginOptions` |
| [formats/interactions/component-capabilities.json](formats/interactions/component-capabilities.json) | Authoritative capability map | Component type classification: `"css-only"`, `"js-only"`, `"both"` |
| [formats/interactions/scripts/generate-capabilities.ts](formats/interactions/scripts/generate-capabilities.ts) | Generates capability map | `hasBehavior()` detection, type inference |

---

### (2) **Current Behavior**

**Flow:**
1. `createComponentsPlugin()` receives a `model: CssDocEntry[]` (merged from @pantoken/components + custom-components)
2. `buildComponentList()` filters for `kind === "component"` or `kind === "custom-component"`, accepts **all**
3. All filtered components are listed in picker dialog; first example HTML is inserted on selection
4. The dialog does **not** currently exclude any components based on whether they're js-only

**Key limitation:** The picker exposes js-only components (date-input, date-time-input, drilldown, icon-button) which:
- Lack standalone CSS—they're interaction behaviors only
- May have non-functional examples in plain HTML (missing JS wiring)
- Semantically belong in a different context (interactive component demo, not static content insertion)

---

### (3) **Recommended Minimal Change: Exclude List Pattern**

**Option A (Static exclude list):**
```typescript
// In components.ts
const JS_ONLY_COMPONENTS = new Set([
  "date-input",
  "date-time-input",
  "drilldown",
  "icon-button",
]);

function buildComponentList(model: CssDocEntry[]): ComponentRecord[] {
  const list: ComponentRecord[] = [];
  for (const entry of model) {
    const kind = entry.kind as string;
    if (kind !== "component" && kind !== "custom-component") continue;
    if (JS_ONLY_COMPONENTS.has(entry.name)) continue; // ← Add exclusion

    list.push({ /* ... */ });
  }
  return list.sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
}
```

**Option B (Configurable via options):**
```typescript
export interface ComponentsPickerOptions {
  model: CssDocEntry[];
  currentAssets: CdnFile[];
  onMissingAsset?: MissingAssetHandler;
  registerUi?: boolean;
  excludeComponents?: Set<string> | string[]; // ← New field
}

function buildComponentList(
  model: CssDocEntry[],
  excludeList?: Set<string> | string[],
): ComponentRecord[] {
  const excluded = excludeList ? new Set(excludeList) : new Set();
  // ... use `excluded.has(entry.name)` to filter
}
```

**Pros & cons:**
- **Static list**: Simple, no config burden, but requires code maintenance when component types change
- **Configurable**: More flexible for downstream integrations, but adds interface complexity

**Future-proof approach:** Load from `component-capabilities.json` at build/runtime:
```typescript
import capabilitiesData from "@pantoken/interactions/component-capabilities.json";

const jsOnlyComponents = new Set(
  capabilitiesData.components
    .filter((c) => c.type === "js-only")
    .map((c) => c.name)
);
```

---

### (4) **Tests & Verification**

**Existing test file:** [renderers/tinymce/tests/components-picker.test.ts](renderers/tinymce/tests/components-picker.test.ts)

**Tests likely needed:**
```typescript
test("picker excludes js-only components (date-input, drilldown, etc.)", () => {
  const plugin = createComponentsPlugin({
    model: [
      { name: "button", kind: "component", examples: [] },
      { name: "date-input", kind: "component", examples: [] }, // js-only
      { name: "drilldown", kind: "component", examples: [] },   // js-only
    ] as any,
    currentAssets: [],
  });

  plugin(editor);
  (editor.ui.registry.addButton as any).mock.calls[0][1].onAction();

  const dialogConfig = (editor.windowManager.open as any).mock.calls[0][0];
  const items = dialogConfig.body.items[0].items;

  expect(items.map((i: any) => i.value)).toEqual(["button"]);
  expect(items.map((i: any) => i.value)).not.toContain("date-input");
  expect(items.map((i: any) => i.value)).not.toContain("drilldown");
});

test("picker respects excludeComponents option", () => {
  const plugin = createComponentsPlugin({
    model: [
      { name: "button", kind: "component", examples: [] },
      { name: "alert", kind: "component", examples: [] },
    ] as any,
    currentAssets: [],
    excludeComponents: ["button"], // Custom exclusion
  });
  // ... assert alert is in list, button is not
});
```

**Verification commands:**
```bash
# Run existing tests
vp test renderers/tinymce

# Run after adding exclude logic
vp test renderers/tinymce --coverage

# Build and type-check
vp check
```

---

### (5) **Ambiguities & Blockers**

| Issue | Status | Resolution |
|-------|--------|-----------|
| **What defines a "generated HTML page"?** | Clarification needed | Likely = components that require JS initialization to function (js-only type) or complex nested DOM layouts (e.g., drawer-layout, menu with submenu) |
| **Should all js-only components be excluded?** | Likely yes | Yes: date-input, date-time-input, drilldown, icon-button all have no CSS component counterpart and require behavior JS |
| **Can CssDocEntry expose component type?** | Not currently | The merged model doesn't carry type metadata from component-capabilities.json; would need to cross-reference or augment CssDocEntry |
| **Who maintains the exclude list?** | Ownership unclear | Should sync with `component-capabilities.json` generation; recommend single source of truth |
| **Does layouts plugin exclude similar components?** | Unknown | Worth checking [renderers/tinymce/src/plugins/layouts.ts](renderers/tinymce/src/plugins/layouts.ts)—if layouts also needs filtering, centralize the logic |
| **Does web-components export metadata about component type?** | Unknown | Worth checking [renderers/web-components/src/lib/elements-meta.ts](renderers/web-components/src/lib/elements-meta.ts) for reusable metadata export |

---

### **Recommended Next Steps**

1. **Determine canonical source of truth** for component types (component-capabilities.json is strong candidate)
2. **Decide on API pattern** (static exclude set vs. configurable via options vs. load from JSON)
3. **Add metadata export** from @pantoken/interactions so tinymce can import `COMPONENTS_REQUIRING_JS` or similar
4. **Implement + test** the filtering logic in buildComponentList
5. **Update docs/comments** explaining why certain components are excluded
6. **Run integration tests** to ensure no unintended side effects on picker UX

